==English==

===Etymology===
From {{inh|en|enm|revisite}}, from {{der|en|frm|revisiter}} and {{der|en|la|revīsitāre}}. {{surf|en|re-|visit}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|en|/ɹiːˈvɪzɪt/}}
* {{audio|en|LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-revisit.wav|a=Southern England}}
*: {{rhymes|en|ɪzɪt|s=3}}

===Verb===
{{en-verb}}

# {{lb|en|transitive}} To [[visit#Verb|visit]] again.
#* {{RQ:Shakespeare Hamlet Q1-2|act=I|scene=iv|sig=C3|page=18|passage=[W]hat may this meane, / That thou, dead corſe, againe in compleate ſteele, / '''Reuiſſits''' thus the glimſes of the Moone, / Making night hideous, and vve fooles of nature, / So horridely to ſhake our diſpoſition, / VVith thoughts beyond the reaches of our ſoules?}}
#* {{quote-book|en|author=[[w:Richard Blackmore|[Richard Blackmore]]]|title=A Hymn to the Light of the World. With a Short Description of the Cartons of [[w:Raphael|Raphael Urbin]], in the Gallery at Hampton-Court|location=London|publisher=Printed for {{w|Jacob Tonson}}{{nb...|within Grays-Inn Gate next Grays-Inn Lane.}}|year=1703|page=8|pageurl=https://books.google.com/books?id=lhphAAAAcAAJ&pg=PA8|oclc=40584794|passage=Thou, Kind Redeemer, toucht to ſee / So ſad a Sight, ſuch moving Miſery, / Didſt ſoon determine to diſpel / Theſe Shades of Death, and Gloom of Hell: / And ſo to '''reviſit''' with Thy Heav'nly Light / Loſt Man, bewilder'd in Infernal Night.}}
# {{lb|en|transitive}} To [[reconsider]] or [[reexperience]] something.

